🔐 Active Directory Account States
Disabled Account

A disabled account still exists in Active Directory but cannot normally be used for authentication.

Possible reasons include:

Employee leaving the organization
Extended leave
Security action
Administrative requirements
Locked Account

A locked account exists in Active Directory but authentication is temporarily blocked, commonly because the user exceeded the configured number of failed login attempts.

Example
Incorrect password
       ↓
Repeated attempts
       ↓
Account Lockout Policy
       ↓
Account Locked
Deleted Account

A deleted account has been removed from Active Directory.

Important distinction
Disabled
↓
Account exists but is disabled

Locked
↓
